# Byte-exactness of the test corpora is the whole point of the oracle /
# fixture tests: several `*.expected` files are LF-terminated plaintext whose
# decoded length is asserted against the archive header. With Git's
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) those files are rewritten to CRLF
# on checkout, which silently changes their size and breaks the assertions.
# Mark every fixture tree — and every fixture extension — as binary so no EOL
# conversion is ever applied, on any platform.
**/tests/data/**       -text
**/tests/fixtures/**   -text
**/benches/data/**     -text
*.expected             -text
*.lzh                  -text
*.raw                  -text
*.lzw                  -text
*.bin                  -text
